<speak>Very much so. I do not mind a missed call if I know we can arrange another time. What I find difficult is answering when I am standing in a lift lobby or trying to greet someone at the office. I would rather have a proper conversation later than give half my attention immediately. Today's arrangement is much better. I have been able to sit still, and even our little digressions have not made me feel that I am neglecting someone waiting outside the door.</speak>